---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CHECKED, COMPETITORS, GITHUB_URL, type Competitor } from '../../data/site';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return COMPETITORS.map((competitor) => ({ params: { slug: competitor.slug }, props: { competitor } }));
}
interface Props {
  competitor: Competitor;
}
const { competitor: c } = Astro.props;
const title = `An open-source, local alternative to ${c.name} | Echo`;
const description = `Echo is a free, open-source alternative to ${c.name} that records, transcribes and summarises meetings on your own Mac, with no bot in the call and no cloud account.`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <span class="kicker">Alternatives</span>
    <h1>An open-source alternative to {c.name}</h1>
    <p>
      {c.name} is a cloud meeting assistant: your meetings are recorded and processed on its servers,
      under an account. Echo does the same core job (recording, transcription, speaker labels and
      notes) entirely on your own Mac.
    </p>

    <h2>How they differ</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Where it runs.</strong> {c.name} is a cloud service. Echo runs on your Mac and listens only on its loopback address.</li>
      <li><strong>In the call.</strong> {c.name}: {c.bot.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + c.bot.slice(1)}. Echo never joins as a participant; its extension records your own meeting tab.</li>
      <li><strong>Your data.</strong> {c.name} stores meetings in {c.storage}. Echo keeps them in an encrypted library on your disk, with the key in the macOS Keychain.</li>
      <li><strong>Price.</strong> {c.name}: {c.price.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + c.price.slice(1)}. Echo is free and open source under the MIT licence.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>When {c.name} is the better fit</h2>
    <p>
      If you need team workspaces, sharing, mobile apps, CRM integrations, or don’t want to run
      software yourself, a hosted service like {c.name} is the simpler choice. Echo is for one person
      on an Apple Silicon Mac who wants their meetings to stay on that Mac.
    </p>

    <h2>Try Echo</h2>
    <p>
      Follow the <a href="/docs/install/">install guide</a> (about ten minutes from a fresh Mac), or
      read the <a href="/#compare">full comparison</a>. The source is on <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Details about {c.name} come from {c.sources.map((s) => <a href={s.url}>{s.label}</a>)}, checked
      on {CHECKED}. Plans change; check {c.name} for current details. {c.name} is a trademark of its
      owner; Echo is not affiliated with it.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
